# UI and Tailwind CSS rules

## Tailwind CSS

- **Use Tailwind classes** - prefer Tailwind classes over custom CSS
- **`@apply` for repeated patterns** - use `@apply` in SCSS only for frequently repeated class combinations
- **Do not use `@apply` for complex gradients** - write complex gradients with fixed pixel values directly in CSS

Example:
```scss
// ❌ Cannot use @apply
.resume-bg {
  background: linear-gradient(
    to bottom,
    #000000 0,
    #80828e 100px,
    #ffffff 400px
  );
}

// ✅ Can use @apply for simple cases
.button {
  @apply px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 text-white;
}
```

## Style structure

- **Do NOT create SCSS files by default** - NEVER create `.component.scss` files when creating a new component; only as a last resort when truly necessary
- **Minimize custom styles** - use SCSS files ONLY when needed (complex gradients, repeated patterns via `@apply`)
- **Remove empty SCSS files** - if a component does not need custom styles, delete the `.component.scss` file
- **Do NOT specify `styleUrls` in the decorator** - if there is no SCSS file, do not specify `styleUrls` in the `@Component` decorator
- **Use inline styles in HTML** - for simple styles, use Tailwind classes directly in templates

## Responsive design

- **Mobile-first approach** - start with mobile styles, then add `md:`, `lg:` prefixes
- **Use breakpoints** - `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` for responsiveness

Example:
```html
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  <!-- Content -->
</div>
```

## UI components

- **Use existing components** - use components from `libs/ui/src/components/` (`@guru/ui` package, e.g. `InputTextComponent`, `InputEmailComponent`)
- **Do not duplicate components** - do not create new components if an equivalent exists in `libs/ui/src/components/`

## Icons and images

- **SVG for icons** - use SVG files from `/assets/img/`
- **`loading="eager"` attribute** - use `loading="eager"` for critical images
- **`alt` attribute** - always specify `alt` for images

Example:
```html
<img
  src="/assets/img/services/vacancies/search.svg"
  alt="Search"
  class="w-5 h-5"
  loading="eager"
/>
```

## HTML formatting

- **2-space indent** - use 2 spaces for indentation in HTML
- **Closing tags** - always close tags, even for self-closing elements in Angular templates
- **Attributes on new lines** - for long attribute lists, wrap onto new lines

Example:
```html
<button
  type="button"
  (click)="onClick()"
  class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg"
  [disabled]="isLoading"
>
  Click me
</button>
```

## Accessibility

- **`sr-only` for hidden labels** - use the `sr-only` class for labels visible only to screen readers
- **`aria-*` attributes** - use `aria-expanded`, `aria-pressed`, and other accessibility attributes

Example:
```html
<label for="search" class="sr-only">Search</label>
<input
  type="text"
  id="search"
  [(ngModel)]="searchQuery"
  placeholder="Search"
/>
```
